\begin{align*}
\frac{\text{number of multiples of }99}{\text{number of four-digit palindromes}}&=\frac{9999}{9999}=\boxed{\frac{1}{1}}.
\end{align*}
Final Answer: The final answer is $\frac{1}{1}$. I hope it is correct.

